# Modularization

> Rendered by `/start` from this repo's `ios-skeleton.config.json` — the tier,
> module graph, and ownership rules below describe **this repo only** (§3.9–§3.11).

## Topology: {{TOPOLOGY_TIER}}

<!-- /start keeps only the block matching the recorded tier. -->

### T1 — single project
One `.xcodeproj`, one app target. No package boundary — everything can see
everything. `Models/`, `Networking/`, `DesignSystem/`, `Core/` are plain folders
inside the app target. `/new-feature` has exactly one destination; there is
nothing to ask.

### T2 — project + local packages *(default)*
One `.xcodeproj` + local Swift packages under `Packages/`: `Core`, `Networking`,
`Models`, `DesignSystem`. A package can't import the app — real compile-time
layering. `Package.resolved` lives at
`App.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/`.

### T3 — workspace + N projects
`{{PRODUCT_NAME}}.xcworkspace` + one project per app/framework. `Package.resolved`
lives at `{{PRODUCT_NAME}}.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/` — it moved off any
single project. The workspace file is emitted by `Scripts/generate_workspace.sh`,
never hand-edited (§3.9's tooling note).

## Module graph

{{MODULE_GRAPH_TABLE}}
<!--
