| Module | Kind | Consumers | Owns |
|---|---|---|---|
| {{AppName}} | app | — | identity, signing, composition root |
| Models | package | {{AppName}} | every model type (§3.2) |
| Networking | package | {{AppName}} | RequestBuilder, APIClient |
| DesignSystem | package | {{AppName}} | base theme tokens, shared states |
-->

**Dependency direction:** apps → shared frameworks/packages → leaf modules. Never
the reverse, never framework → app, never app → app (§3.9). Enforced by
`/add-module`'s hard refusal on a cycle.

## Ownership rules from T2 onward (§3.11)

- **Localization is per resource-owning module, not per repo.** Every module
  with UI owns its own `Localization/Localizable.strings` (+ translations) and a
  **bundle-aware** generated `L10n.swift` — never `Bundle.main` from inside a
  shared module. Keys are namespaced by module (`shared.error.retry`,
  `{{APP_NAMESPACE}}.settings.title`).
- **Theme is base + override, not one file.** Base tokens live in
  {{BASE_THEME_MODULE}}'s `Theme/`; each app's own thin `Theme/` overrides only
  what differs. `/update-theme` enforces this split.
- **Assets, icons, permissions and identity are per app, always.** `AppIcon`,
  `Info.plist`, `.entitlements`, bundle ID, display name and signing never live
  in a shared module.

## `/new-feature`'s default destination

{{#if SINGLE_APP}}
This repo has one app (`{{DEFAULT_MODULE}}`) — `--module` is optional, everything
lands there.
{{else}}
This repo has more than one app/module. `/new-feature` resolves its destination
as: an explicit `--module` argument → the config's declared default
(`{{DEFAULT_MODULE}}`, if set) → **stop and ask**. It never guesses (§3.11, §4).
{{/if}}
